+// The game loop calls THPPlayerDrawDone every frame, and retail waits there (GXDrawDone) until the GPU
+// has drawn the whole frame, so that the movie's texture sets drawn in it can be decoded into again.
+// On the 3DS the GX thread draws beside the game: that wait idled the game thread ~7 ms a frame at
+// Delfino Plaza, whose TV plays a movie all the time. A texture set's memory is free once the GX
+// thread has run past the draw that read it (the renderer keeps its own copy of the texture), so
+// used sets are parked, each with the stream position after its frame, and go back to the free
+// queue once the GX thread has passed it. sms3ds_gx_mark / sms3ds_gx_reached:
+// platform3ds/gx3ds/gxthread.cpp.
+#ifdef __cplusplus
